{title: 532 - Day by Day}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #532 • BLOTT EN DAG • 10.8.10.9.9.10.10.7}
{lyricist: Carolina Sandell Berg}
{composer: Oscar Ahnfelt}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 532}
{meta: tune BLOTT EN DAG}
{meta: meter 10.8.10.9.9.10.10.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Day by day, and with each passing moment,
[G]Strength I find to [A7]meet my trials here;
[D]Trusting in my Father's wise [G]bestowment,
[A]I've no cause for worry [D]or for fear.
[D/F#]He, whose heart is kind beyond [A7/G]all [G]measure,
[Em]Gives unto [A7]each day what [D]He [A7]deems best,
[Bm]Lovingly [D/A]its part of [G]pain and [E7/G#]pleasure,
[A]Mingling toil with [A7]peace and [D]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Every day, the Lord Himself is near me
[G]With a special [A7]mercy for each hour;
[D]All my cares He fain would bear, [G]and cheer me,
[A]He whose name is Counselor [D]and power.
[D/F#]The protection of His [A7/G]child [G]and [F#m]treasure
[Em]Is a [A7]charge that on Himself He laid;
[Bm]As your [D/A]days, your strength shall [G]be in [E7/G#]measure,
[A]This the pledge to [A7]me He [D]made.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Help me then in every tribulation
[G]So to trust Thy [A7]promises, O Lord,
[D]That I lose not faith's sweet consolation
[A]Offered me within Thy [D]holy Word.
[D/F#]Help me, Lord, when toil and [A7/G]trouble [F#m]meeting,
[Em]E'er to [A7]take, as from a [D]father's [A7]hand,
[Bm]One by [D/A]one, the days, the [G]moments [E7/G#]fleeting,
[A]Till I reach the [A7]promised [D]land.
{end_of_verse}
